WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.900
World Masterpiece Theater

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
Homeless Child Remy

00:07.800 --> 00:14.400
"About Love"

00:15.260 --> 00:23.160
I continue wishing to see you

00:23.690 --> 00:28.360
Today we'll go on a journey

00:28.450 --> 00:32.310
That's as endless as the blue sky

00:32.820 --> 00:40.990
With joy, sorrow and hope come setbacks

00:41.360 --> 00:46.040
They repeat, they repeat

00:46.280 --> 00:50.870
What should I believe?

00:51.510 --> 00:59.880
You know nothing about love, however

01:00.320 --> 01:08.900
Someday you will feel warmth inside

01:09.730 --> 01:19.860
I dream of the day when you'll speak of love

01:20.860 --> 01:28.660
Tomorrow, our journey will begin

01:29.510 --> 01:35.000
Presented by:
Takara Fansubs & Migoto

01:35.020 --> 01:39.800
Episode 19:
A Traveling Family

01:43.660 --> 01:46.870
Remy, how did it go today?
- Not good.

01:47.360 --> 01:50.230
Very few people came to see me.

01:50.420 --> 01:54.080
Joli-Coeur and Capi are doing their best though.

01:54.500 --> 01:56.840
I'll get scolded by the boss.

01:57.230 --> 02:01.340
Tomorrow will be fine.
- Yeah, it will go fine.

02:01.670 --> 02:03.360
Huh, why?

02:04.790 --> 02:07.350
A special market place will be open tomorrow.

02:07.990 --> 02:10.110
A big one.

02:10.280 --> 02:14.850
If you perform an interesting show, a lot of people will come.

02:15.440 --> 02:16.740
I see.

02:17.470 --> 02:20.510
Are you guys going too?
- Yeah, we go every year.

02:20.530 --> 02:24.100
It's a good place to make money.
- Wow… I should do my best, too.

02:24.190 --> 02:25.360
Yeah.

02:28.340 --> 02:33.630
Mary, you must be tired from walking all day long.

02:34.150 --> 02:35.320
I'm all right.

02:35.810 --> 02:37.220
Hang in there.

02:37.310 --> 02:42.710
In Toulouse, Arthur and the madam have been waiting for good news.

02:42.710 --> 02:44.620
Yes, I know.

02:45.150 --> 02:52.960
But I'm a bit worried if I can really find Remy in this big city.

02:52.960 --> 02:54.570
Don't give up.

02:55.030 --> 02:56.860
Let's go to the market place.

02:57.060 --> 02:58.070
Market place?

02:58.270 --> 03:02.040
Yes, there will be a big market, opened for a week.

03:02.170 --> 03:06.070
Every year, many merchants and street performers come from all over.

03:07.080 --> 03:10.960
If Remy and Mr. Vitalis are in Paris, they will surely come and show their performances.

03:12.020 --> 03:13.580
If so, it will be great.

03:21.850 --> 03:26.300
<i>Madam and Arthur, did you hear that?</i>

03:26.440 --> 03:31.310
<i>If what Mr. Blair said is true, I will have a great chance to find Remy.</i>

03:32.450 --> 03:38.800
<i>Yes, I will definitely find Remy... for sure.</i>

03:52.820 --> 03:56.280
This is the best quality silk fabric.

03:56.300 --> 03:58.960
It's a rare quality.

03:59.260 --> 04:04.480
I carry anything: Oriental pearls, corals, diamonds and emeralds.

04:04.750 --> 04:06.710
Madam, I will give you a discount.

04:06.800 --> 04:09.670
You will give me more discounts, won't you?

04:10.500 --> 04:14.200
Look, it's great, isn’t it, Remy? There's everything here.

04:14.470 --> 04:18.240
There are shops that sell little birds and insects over there.

04:18.390 --> 04:20.920
And ones that sell candies and chocolate over there.

04:21.480 --> 04:24.760
It's a good business place for us, too.

04:24.830 --> 04:26.500
We can make good money.

04:26.570 --> 04:28.700
Guys, let's do our best.
- Yeah!

04:29.120 --> 04:33.910
All right, I'll do my best.
Capi, Joli-Coeur, I'm counting on you.

04:47.970 --> 04:50.240
Wow, what a great turnout.

04:50.830 --> 04:53.430
It'll be here for a week.

04:53.830 --> 04:56.430
I wonder if I can find Remy here.

04:56.810 --> 04:59.870
Let's hope that we do find her.
- Yes.

04:59.940 --> 05:01.990
Thank you very much, Mr. Blair.

05:02.580 --> 05:04.500
Wow, there's so many people.

05:04.570 --> 05:07.190
Is there any good place?

05:07.280 --> 05:08.820
Vitalis?

05:09.240 --> 05:12.220
I haven't seen him for quite a long time.

05:12.260 --> 05:16.800
I see.
If you see Mr. Vitalis, please let us know.

05:16.820 --> 05:19.030
Yeah, I understand.

05:20.080 --> 05:22.310
What's wrong, Mary?

05:22.330 --> 05:24.710
Oh... Nothing.

05:33.130 --> 05:34.120
Hey.

05:35.620 --> 05:37.830
Are you going to do something here?

05:39.350 --> 05:43.230
You're a street performer, aren't you?
If you do some performances...

05:43.930 --> 05:45.440
What makes you think that?

05:45.830 --> 05:48.430
Because of the tambourine.

05:51.670 --> 05:53.780
I'm not a street performer.

05:55.510 --> 05:57.330
She's a bit strange.

06:00.620 --> 06:02.290
We'll take this spot.

06:04.190 --> 06:05.250
Oh...

06:09.680 --> 06:12.260
It looks exactly like Mr. Vitalis's horse cart.

06:44.280 --> 06:47.040
<i>Mr. Vitalis, I'm all right.</i>

06:47.100 --> 06:50.870
<i>I've been doing good with Joli-Coeur and Capi.</i>

06:54.200 --> 06:57.020
Okay, Capi. Let's go now.

06:58.810 --> 07:02.180
What a wonderful dog and a cute monkey.

07:02.180 --> 07:03.680
Are you a street performer?

07:03.830 --> 07:04.720
Yes.

07:04.850 --> 07:08.860
I do plays and dances with Capi and Joli-Coeur.

07:11.950 --> 07:14.020
So do we.

07:14.020 --> 07:17.210
We came from Lyon to show our performances here.

07:17.210 --> 07:20.810
This girl looks the same age as Cosette.

07:21.000 --> 07:22.500
What is your name?

07:23.410 --> 07:24.270
I'm Remy.

07:24.660 --> 07:27.750
It's impressive that you do performances by yourself.

07:29.070 --> 07:32.770
On the other hand, our child, Cosette...

07:33.040 --> 07:35.820
Dear, now's not the time to talk of such a thing...

07:35.820 --> 07:37.780
Oh... Right.

07:38.400 --> 07:39.740
I'm sorry...

07:39.870 --> 07:42.160
I'm sorry for talking about something so boring.

07:42.160 --> 07:43.780
Oh... No...

07:44.150 --> 07:46.350
We'll be going now.

07:46.350 --> 07:47.760
Must you?

07:47.760 --> 07:49.260
Cosette.

07:49.720 --> 07:51.440
You're the girl I met...

07:52.060 --> 07:55.680
Oh... You two know each other.

08:02.110 --> 08:04.670
My name is Remy. Nice to meet you.

08:05.000 --> 08:08.280
These are my friends, Joli-Coeur and Capi.

08:11.390 --> 08:13.770
Is this your house?

08:13.840 --> 08:18.800
How nice. You travel with your father and mother in this house cart.

08:19.170 --> 08:20.830
It isn't nice.

08:21.020 --> 08:24.570
Huh?
- I'm fed up with traveling.

08:24.570 --> 08:28.300
I hate playing, singing and dancing.

08:29.770 --> 08:30.810
Why?

08:31.600 --> 08:33.520
It's none of your business.

08:47.720 --> 08:50.540
I like living in a horse cart.

09:02.370 --> 09:03.980
What's wrong?

09:09.580 --> 09:13.000
Oh... Sorry. I was remembering when I used to travel.

09:13.420 --> 09:15.420
You were traveling, too?

09:15.800 --> 09:18.420
Yeah, with Mr. Vitalis.

09:19.460 --> 09:22.590
But the horse cart burned in a fire.

09:22.740 --> 09:24.370
Fire?
- Yeah.

09:35.080 --> 09:38.020
Are you alone?
- No...

09:38.570 --> 09:42.640
Now I live in my boss Gaspard's house with my friends.

09:43.150 --> 09:46.260
I'm not alone because I have Capi and Joli-Coeur, too.

09:49.630 --> 09:52.510
Oh... The performance is about to start, right?

09:52.530 --> 09:53.590
Seems like it.

09:54.000 --> 09:55.400
You should go, too.

09:55.800 --> 09:56.910
No.

10:00.170 --> 10:04.490
You shouldn't say that. I've been through a hard time, too.

10:04.490 --> 10:08.320
But I think it's wonderful to sing a song or do plays together.

10:08.370 --> 10:08.870
Hmmph.

10:09.120 --> 10:13.110
Cosette! Cosette! Come on. Please, come here!

10:13.940 --> 10:15.420
Your mother is calling you.

10:15.970 --> 10:17.620
Quit being nosey.

10:19.650 --> 10:22.450
Cosette!
- Cosette!

10:23.400 --> 10:25.210
Please come, Cosette!

10:26.790 --> 10:30.170
I wonder what Cosette is going to do.

10:51.300 --> 10:58.000
Hello, people of the market. The Michelle troupe's show is about to begin.

11:01.110 --> 11:02.440
Dear...

11:02.810 --> 11:04.680
It's no use.

11:04.770 --> 11:09.030
Cosette's dance is the highlight of the Michelle troupe's show.

11:09.090 --> 11:12.020
Without her, no one shows up.

11:12.750 --> 11:19.500
We've been really busy recently, so she's been acting selfish.

11:20.400 --> 11:23.530
Everyone! The fun performance starring Capi and Joli-Coeur,

11:23.600 --> 11:27.160
of Michelle troupe, is about to begin!

11:32.390 --> 11:36.270
Let me help you.
Capi and Joli-Coeur will join us, too.

11:43.170 --> 11:46.500
<i>No! No way.</i>

11:49.490 --> 11:52.010
Look, I'm all sold out.

11:52.490 --> 11:53.530
Me, too.

11:53.590 --> 11:57.430
We've earned a lot.
Today's the best, isn't it?

12:22.490 --> 12:24.850
Dear...
- Yeah...

12:25.160 --> 12:28.620
Are those people Remy's acquaintances?

12:28.840 --> 12:32.100
Remy is doing a great job.

12:32.100 --> 12:36.620
Smart dog, isn't it?
- Look at the monkey's proud face.

12:36.730 --> 12:39.620
That girl's performance is great, too.
- Good job!

12:55.620 --> 12:59.100
Remy, thank you.
- Thanks to you there were so many people.

12:59.190 --> 13:01.570
I have to thank you guys, too.

13:03.800 --> 13:06.040
Here's your share.

13:06.040 --> 13:06.970
Thank you.

13:09.400 --> 13:13.030
This much?
- Because the audience was so generous.

13:13.030 --> 13:16.030
Please, take it.
- Thank you very much.

13:16.030 --> 13:18.850
Remy, why don't we do this together tomorrow, too?

13:18.850 --> 13:22.580
If you do, it will be a big help for us.
- Okay.

13:22.580 --> 13:24.380
Give me guidance.

13:24.380 --> 13:28.480
Sure... And do the same for us.
- Here's some candy. Have some.

13:28.480 --> 13:30.970
Cosette, have some, too.

13:37.120 --> 13:38.600
Delicious.

13:44.090 --> 13:45.760
Delicious.

13:45.760 --> 13:49.890
I can die any time.
- You're overreacting, Jacques.

13:49.890 --> 13:52.750
But this is the first time I've eaten something so delicious.

13:52.820 --> 13:53.570
Me too.

13:53.720 --> 13:57.730
I wish I could eat it every day.
- That's impossible.

13:57.860 --> 14:00.550
Right... Then I'll savor it.

14:01.060 --> 14:04.570
Huh, those guys are so happy with those candies.

14:05.010 --> 14:08.620
Huh? Did you say something?
- I didn't say anything.

14:10.560 --> 14:14.480
Say, has Remy been living with you for a long time?

14:14.550 --> 14:19.250
Yeah, we've been together since last winter. We've been good friends.

14:19.440 --> 14:21.180
Oh no! There's the boss!

14:24.510 --> 14:27.970
Oh no! If he sees what we're doing, we will be punished.

14:28.460 --> 14:30.020
Let's go!

14:31.830 --> 14:34.230
Mattia, what should we do?

14:34.720 --> 14:37.010
Boss Gaspard!

14:38.000 --> 14:40.930
Oh... What are you guys goofing off for?

14:41.070 --> 14:42.230
Not good. Let's go!

14:52.310 --> 14:53.520
I'm sorry!

15:05.000 --> 15:06.330
What's wrong?

15:06.330 --> 15:09.760
That, that girl is Remy!
- Huh?

15:10.620 --> 15:12.450
Let's go!
- Yes.

15:14.610 --> 15:19.440
Phew, that was a close one.
- But we're safe now, aren't we?

15:19.440 --> 15:21.580
Big brother Mattia!

15:22.390 --> 15:23.960
Mattia, there's trouble!

15:27.620 --> 15:30.880
Remy was caught by the boss!
- Huh?

15:30.880 --> 15:33.060
She was taken to the park.

15:33.200 --> 15:35.110
What should we do, Mattia?

15:35.550 --> 15:38.200
I'll go. You guys go home now.

15:39.120 --> 15:43.550
Even though you could be making good money, you're just playing around!

15:43.550 --> 15:45.490
I wasn't playing around!

15:45.780 --> 15:48.140
Shut up!

15:53.050 --> 15:55.350
Why you...
- Stop!

15:56.820 --> 16:00.390
I've already earned enough!
- What did you say?

16:03.150 --> 16:04.340
Hmph...

16:07.840 --> 16:11.170
Oh... You've earned a lot, haven't you?

16:11.260 --> 16:13.360
But it's not enough.

16:13.530 --> 16:16.640
Huh?
- Earn another 20 sous.

16:16.640 --> 16:19.950
No way!
- Shut up!

16:21.000 --> 16:23.890
That's your punishment for confusing me.

16:23.890 --> 16:26.890
20 sous more. Do you understand?

16:32.620 --> 16:35.480
I'm all right, I'm all right.

16:40.420 --> 16:43.490
I... I...

16:43.640 --> 16:47.590
I was trying to get Remy in trouble... Just a little bit...

16:47.720 --> 16:51.420
But then it turned out like this...
- Remy was a foundling.

16:52.410 --> 16:53.490
A foundling?

16:53.630 --> 16:57.660
Remy was sold to a child merchant by her foster parent.

16:57.660 --> 17:01.490
And the person who saved her from him was Vitalis, the traveling performer.

17:01.960 --> 17:05.990
Since then they had been traveling throughout the country.

17:06.340 --> 17:09.500
I heard it was not an easy journey.

17:18.160 --> 17:20.030
Well, we have to go and make more money.

17:20.520 --> 17:21.730
Let's go.

17:23.160 --> 17:26.000
And then, Mr. Vitalis passed away.

17:26.180 --> 17:32.400
Mr. Vitalis, please don't leave me alone.

17:33.390 --> 17:36.340
Don't, don't die.

17:53.620 --> 17:57.060
So Remy came to Paris alone.

17:58.100 --> 18:03.280
She's not the only one...
It's not an unusual story.

18:03.650 --> 18:06.830
We all have the same kind of background.

18:12.380 --> 18:15.400
Tell me what kind of girl Remy is!

18:15.930 --> 18:18.900
Mr. Vitalis told her...

18:20.430 --> 18:22.920
Remy, you're a cheerful girl.

18:23.110 --> 18:29.400
Don't lose it. Cheerfulness is strength and hope.

18:29.810 --> 18:33.740
But you can't survive in Paris with that optimistic mind.

18:34.180 --> 18:39.430
But she still follows it earnestly, believes in it...

18:40.420 --> 18:44.380
Even when she wants to cry during hard times.

18:44.380 --> 18:46.080
That's Remy.

18:50.530 --> 18:52.580
<i>Cheerfulness is strength.</i>

18:53.090 --> 18:55.450
<i>Cheerfulness is hope.</i>

19:17.580 --> 19:20.510
Remy!
- Oh, Cosette.

19:22.080 --> 19:24.900
Remy, I heard it from your friend.

19:25.050 --> 19:27.410
Huh?
- I was watching.

19:27.810 --> 19:31.000
I'm sorry that happened to you because of me.

19:32.610 --> 19:35.500
It is not a big deal. Oh...

19:35.900 --> 19:38.500
I have to keep working.

19:38.560 --> 19:41.230
I'll help you.
- Cosette.

19:41.490 --> 19:44.890
But I feel bad for you.
- Please, let me help you.

19:51.170 --> 19:54.870
Okay, thank you.
- Great.

19:59.080 --> 20:01.880
Mary!
- How did it go, Mr. Blair?

20:04.240 --> 20:05.940
I see.

20:08.740 --> 20:09.860
<i>Remy...</i>

20:12.550 --> 20:16.010
Thank you, Cosette. You were a big help.

20:16.120 --> 20:19.960
I envy you.
- Huh? Why?

20:20.330 --> 20:23.020
Because you have such a good friend.

20:23.330 --> 20:26.950
Cosette, you have a wonderful father and mother.

20:28.880 --> 20:31.310
Remy was a foundling.

20:33.360 --> 20:37.790
I didn't want to be a traveling performer anymore.

20:37.920 --> 20:40.060
I wanted to live in a house.

20:40.280 --> 20:44.360
I wanted to go to school and talk and play with my friends.

20:45.060 --> 20:47.240
I thought it was impossible to make friends,

20:47.350 --> 20:50.640
if I was living my life traveling all over.

20:52.800 --> 20:55.000
We're friends.

20:55.310 --> 20:58.420
Friends?
- Yup.  We're friends already.

20:59.020 --> 21:00.380
Remy...

21:03.580 --> 21:06.350
Thank you. Thank you, Remy.

21:06.710 --> 21:08.400
I'll come earlier tomorrow.

21:08.430 --> 21:11.380
I'll be waiting. I'll be waiting. Okay?

21:19.820 --> 21:24.600
It was not an illusion.
It was surely Remy.

21:24.690 --> 21:27.380
Mary, it was a good thing.

21:28.710 --> 21:32.580
At least we've found out that Remy is in Paris.

21:32.740 --> 21:34.520
It was great progress.

21:36.310 --> 21:38.010
That's right, isn't it?

21:38.730 --> 21:47.330
Try to love yourself more

21:40.250 --> 21:47.000
<i>Remy, I will find you for sure and take you to your mother.</i>

21:47.350 --> 21:51.430
<i>Until then, please wait, Remy.</i>

21:48.360 --> 21:57.710
Abandoned dreams can be seen again

21:57.870 --> 22:07.060
Surely, not everyone can be so strong

22:07.520 --> 22:18.630
The blue sky lifts all of the world's tears...

22:18.920 --> 22:28.770
Tomorrow's courage comes

22:28.880 --> 22:38.600
From the future that gives us our fate

22:38.710 --> 22:47.830
Try to seek for them more

22:48.300 --> 22:52.110
Give your heart to

22:52.200 --> 23:09.020
That person who is also seeking you

23:18.230 --> 23:20.220
Hey, Remy, let's go together.
- Huh?

23:20.520 --> 23:23.590
I've been thinking that it would be great if you'd become a member of our family.

23:23.850 --> 23:25.840
I can't do that.

23:25.920 --> 23:30.090
No! If Remy goes, then big brother Mattia will be gone, too!

23:30.150 --> 23:33.240
I'll be all alone!

23:33.350 --> 23:36.680
<i>Soul Mate</i>

23:33.350 --> 23:36.680
Next time:
